---
/**
 * florist / PageBT — "Gumamela" (a loud, colourful florist template; the
 * handoff's sample shop is a Cebu florist).
 *
 * Light and loud: Bricolage Grotesque display at weight 800 over Instrument
 * Sans on a warm paper ground, a hard 2px ink rule around every card, and two
 * saturated fills doing all the shouting: the red and the marigold. Full-bleed
 * bands alternate paper, red, marigold and ink down the page.
 *
 * ROLE OF THIS FILE: the wrapper emits the WHOLE document (doctype, head,
 * tokens, fonts, Leaflet boot, skip link). It does NOT compose with
 * BaseLayout. It is the only file in the variant that touches `siteData`; the
 * section components receive only `layout` and `content`.
 *
 * EDITABLE HOOKS OWNED BY THIS FILE: none. It only READS layout.businessName
 * and layout.tagline (the title element), content.description (the meta
 * description), layout.favicon and layout.ogImage. Every data-field,
 * data-image-field and data-href-field hook lives in a section component.
 * Section visibility is the camelCase visibility keys below, each tested
 * `!== false`, one section per line, in the design's order.
 *
 * THE ONE HARDCODED VISIBLE STRING is the skip link's "Skip to content", an
 * a11y affordance visible on focus only (PageBJ precedent).
 *
 * DESIGN ISOLATION: every selector in the global block is prefixed
 * html[data-page="BT"], including the reset, body, a, summary and the base
 * primitives. index.astro bundles every wrapper's global CSS onto every page,
 * so an unanchored rule here would repaint every other template.
 *
 * TOKEN PLAN. The design's colours map onto the theme engine's vocabulary by
 * ROLE, so an explicit admin colour pick recolours the whole page coherently:
 *   paper    #FBF1EC  -> --paper      (ground; the text colour on ink bands)
 *   blush    #F4E1D8  -> --paper-2    (trust cells, review cards, FAQ band)
 *   white    #FFFFFF  -> --card       (shop cards)
 *   ink      #2B1015  -> --ink        (text, every 2px rule, the ink bands)
 *   muted    #6A4A4E  -> --ink-soft and --muted (body copy)
 *   red      #C21E3A  -> --accent     (eyebrows, headline emphasis, red fills)
 *   marigold #F2B233  -> --accent-light (marigold fills, labels on ink)
 *   on-red   #FFF4F0  -> --on-primary (the label on every red fill; the engine
 *                       picks it from the scheme's primary, which is exactly
 *                       what --accent becomes)
 * Six ROLE tokens carry names the engine does not know, on purpose, so the
 * wrapper can keep them legible when a pick moves the colours around them:
 *   --accent-text   the red used as TEXT on a light ground (eyebrows, the
 *                   hero's emphasised phrase, reason numerals, stars, the FAQ
 *                   +, link hovers). Natively it IS --accent.
 *   --on-red-soft   #FFE3DC, the design's body tint on the red How band.
 *   --on-red-label  the marigold "Step N" labels on the red band (and an <em>
 *                   in its headline). Natively it IS --accent-light.
 *   --on-mari-accent the red as TEXT on a marigold fill (the drawer's link
 *                   hover, an <em> in the Why and CTA headlines). Natively it
 *                   IS --accent.
 *   --drawer-hover-bg the drawer link's hover fill. Natively transparent.
 *   --on-ink-hover  the red link hover on the ink location card (the phone).
 *                   Natively it IS --accent.
 * Only __schemeCss moves them, and only under an explicit admin scheme: on the
 * red band both follow the engine's --on-primary pick (the design's tints are
 * only legible on the design's red; a scheme's light accent on its primary
 * measures 2.3-2.9:1 even mixed 40%). A scheme's primary on its own light
 * accent measures 1.5-2.2:1, so --on-mari-accent becomes --ink and the drawer
 * hover gains a --paper fill (a label change alone would be invisible). On the
 * ink card the phone hover takes the light accent (4.2-6.4:1, against 2.1 for
 * brown's primary). On a DARK-paper scheme (maroon, dark, black)
 * --accent-text becomes the scheme's light accent mixed toward --ink —
 * maroon's primary measures 1.7:1 on its own paper, which would erase the
 * hero's red phrase and every eyebrow.
 * The paper-alpha washes on the ink bands are built from --paper-rgb, so they
 * follow a pick. Text sitting ON a marigold fill is --ink, never --on-accent:
 * the engine picks --on-accent from the scheme's light accent and returns white
 * for pink, which would strand a white label on a pale pink band.
 *
 * FONT-PAIRING SENTINEL (verbatim from PageBJ): lib/astro-builder.ts defaults
 * layout.fontPairing to the literal 'modern', and resolveTheme's lockVariant
 * only blanks ''/'auto'/'default', so without the sentinel buildOverrideCss
 * force-swaps Space Grotesk and Inter onto nearly every real site. The
 * builder's DEFAULT is treated as unset; a deliberate admin pick still applies.
 *
 * FORBIDDEN CLASS NAMES (lib/genericThemeOverrides.ts pins them):
 *   .btn-primary .btn-ghost .btn-yellow .btn-light .nav-cta .nav-right
 *   .testi .cta-band .trust, and `hero` as a class on any element.
 * Buttons here are .btn with a double-dash variant (.btn--fill .btn--line
 * .btn--mari .btn--ink .btn--paper). Every variant declares its own fill and
 * restates fill AND label on hover. The footer carries no .btn at all.
 *
 * RENDER ORDER, exactly as the design draws it: Header, Hero (#top), Marquee
 * (#marquee), Trust, Services (#services, plus the #events band it owns),
 * About (#about), Why (#why), Gallery (#gallery), How (#how), Testimonials
 * (#reviews), Credentials (#credentials), Area (#area), Faq (#faq), Location
 * (#visit), then the CtaBand (#book) outside main, Footer, and the floating
 * message pill.
 *
 * NO MOTION the design does not have: no scroll reveal, no hover transitions.
 * Smooth anchor scrolling is the design's own and drops to auto under
 * prefers-reduced-motion.
 *
 * Leaflet: this wrapper loads leaflet.css and leaflet.js and defines
 * window.__floristBTInitMap (family-unique). LocationBT calls that exact
 * name when Leaflet is already loaded, and otherwise leaves its args on
 * window.__floristBTMapArgs, which the boot drains once leaflet.js has
 * loaded (no retry timer to outlast). The boot empties the map element before
 * mounting, which is what erases the drawn fallback face, and the element
 * keeps the literal id "map".
 */
import HeaderBT from './header/HeaderBT.astro';
import HeroBT from './hero/HeroBT.astro';
import MarqueeBT from './marquee/MarqueeBT.astro';
import TrustBT from './trust/TrustBT.astro';
import ServicesBT from './services/ServicesBT.astro';
import AboutBT from './about/AboutBT.astro';
import WhyBT from './why/WhyBT.astro';
import GalleryBT from './gallery/GalleryBT.astro';
import HowBT from './how/HowBT.astro';
import TestimonialsBT from './testimonials/TestimonialsBT.astro';
import CredentialsBT from './credentials/CredentialsBT.astro';
import AreaBT from './area/AreaBT.astro';
import FaqBT from './faq/FaqBT.astro';
import LocationBT from './location/LocationBT.astro';
import CtaBandBT from './ctaBand/CtaBandBT.astro';
import FooterBT from './footer/FooterBT.astro';
import { resolveTheme, buildFontHref, buildOverrideCss } from '../../lib/genericThemeOverrides';

interface Props { siteData: any; }
const { siteData } = Astro.props;
const layout = siteData.layout ?? {};
const content = siteData.content ?? {};
const visibility = siteData.visibility ?? {};
const title = layout.businessName
  ? `${layout.businessName}${layout.tagline ? ' — ' + layout.tagline : ''}`
  : 'Welcome';
const { scheme: __themeScheme, pairing: __resolvedPairing } = resolveTheme(layout, (content as any).business_type, { lockVariant: true });
// 'modern' is astro-builder's DEFAULT, not a choice (lib/astro-builder.ts).
// Treating it as unset keeps Bricolage Grotesque; a deliberate admin pick applies.
const __themePairing = __resolvedPairing === 'modern' ? '' : __resolvedPairing;
const __overrideCss = buildOverrideCss(__themeScheme, __themePairing);
const __fontHref = buildFontHref(__themePairing);
// Wrapper-side palette fix, gated on the SCHEME (never on __overrideCss, which a
// font pick alone makes non-empty) — see the TOKEN PLAN above. Natively this is
// empty and every role token equals the design's own colour.
// html:root[data-page] outranks the token block's html[data-page], so this wins
// wherever the bundler places the global stylesheet relative to this tag.
const __darkScheme = ['maroon', 'dark', 'black'].includes(__themeScheme);
const __schemeCss = __themeScheme
  ? 'html:root[data-page="BT"]{'
    + '--on-red-soft:var(--on-primary);'
    + '--on-red-label:var(--on-primary);'
    + '--on-mari-accent:var(--ink);'
    + '--drawer-hover-bg:var(--paper);'
    + '--on-ink-hover:var(--accent-light);'
    + (__darkScheme ? '--accent-text:color-mix(in srgb,var(--accent-light) 55%,var(--ink));' : '')
    + '}'
  : '';
---

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en" data-page="BT">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8" />
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
  <title>{title}</title>
  {content.description && <meta name="description" content={content.description} />}
  <!-- Browser-chrome tint. A meta tag cannot read a CSS var, so this repeats the
       paper ground token (--paper) the sticky header sits on. -->
  <meta name="theme-color" content="#FBF1EC" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
  <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin="" />
  <!-- The design's native faces, exactly as its helmet loads them:
       Bricolage Grotesque on its optical-size axis at 500-800, and Instrument
       Sans at 400/500/600/700. -->
  <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Bricolage+Grotesque:opsz,wght@12..96,500..800&family=Instrument+Sans:wght@400;500;600;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet" />
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.css" integrity="sha256-p4NxAoJBhIIN+hmNHrzRCf9tD/miZyoHS5obTRR9BMY=" crossorigin="" />
  {layout.favicon && <link rel="icon" href={layout.favicon} />}
  {(layout.ogImage || layout.favicon) && <meta property="og:image" content={layout.ogImage || layout.favicon} />}

  <style is:global>
    /* ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       PageBT · "Gumamela" — florist. Tokens + shared base primitives. EVERY
       selector is prefixed html[data-page="BT"].

       FOUR LOAD-BEARING FACTS. Do not "tidy" any of them:

       1. SPECIFICITY. Every appearance-bearing base primitive is wrapped in
          :where(), so an Astro-scoped section rule always wins over it.

       2. BUTTONS. .btn plus one double-dash variant. Each variant states its
          own fill, border and label, and its :hover restates all three, so a
          label can never strand mid-hover. No transitions: the design's hover
          states are instant.

       3. FOCUS. One duo ring for everything: a 3px paper outline inside a
          6px ink halo, legible on paper, on the red and marigold fills and on
          the ink bands alike.

       4. HEAD ORDER. This block is followed by the admin font link and then,
          LAST in the head, the engine's override block. Its html:root rules
          only beat these tokens because they come later in source order.
          (Never write a literal closing style tag inside this block, comments
          included: the parser would end the stylesheet right there.)
    ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ */

    html[data-page="BT"] {
      /* grounds */
      --paper: #FBF1EC;
      --paper-2: #F4E1D8;
      --card: #FFFFFF;
      /* ink: text, every 2px rule, and the ground of the ink bands */
      --ink: #2B1015;
      --ink-soft: #6A4A4E;
      --muted: #6A4A4E;
      --line: rgba(43,16,21,.18);
      /* the two loud fills */
      --accent: #C21E3A;
      --accent-light: #F2B233;
      /* rgb triplets for the alpha washes */
      --paper-rgb: 251,241,236;
      --ink-rgb: 43,16,21;
      --accent-rgb: 194,30,58;
      /* contrast aliases the override engine and inherited rules expect.
         --on-primary is the label on a red (--accent) fill; --on-accent pairs
         with --accent-light, exactly as the engine derives it. */
      --on-primary: #FFF4F0;
      --on-accent: #2B1015;
      --on-ink: #FBF1EC;
      --on-paper: #2B1015;
      /* ROLE tokens the engine does not know, on purpose — see the TOKEN PLAN
         in the frontmatter. Natively each is exactly the design's colour. */
      --accent-text: var(--accent);
      --on-red-soft: #FFE3DC;
      --on-red-label: var(--accent-light);
      --on-mari-accent: var(--accent);
      --drawer-hover-bg: transparent;
      --on-ink-hover: var(--accent);
      /* type */
      /* The design's own stacks, verbatim: the fallback matters, because the
         marquee's separator glyph is not in Bricolage and is drawn by it. */
      --disp: "Bricolage Grotesque", sans-serif;
      --sans: "Instrument Sans", system-ui, sans-serif;
      --serif: "Bricolage Grotesque", sans-serif;
      --mono: "Instrument Sans", system-ui, sans-serif;
      /* metrics */
      --maxw: 1280px;
      --gutter: clamp(18px,4vw,48px);
    }

    /* ── reset + document ─────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    html[data-page="BT"] *,
    html[data-page="BT"] *::before,
    html[data-page="BT"] *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }
    html[data-page="BT"] {
      -webkit-text-size-adjust: 100%;
      scroll-behavior: smooth;
      /* The sticky header is 74px (72px bar + its 2px rule); every in-page
         anchor lands 12px clear of it. */
      scroll-padding-top: 86px;
    }
    @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { html[data-page="BT"] { scroll-behavior: auto; } }
    html[data-page="BT"] body {
      margin: 0; padding: 0;
      background-color: var(--paper); color: var(--ink);
      font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 17px; line-height: 1.6;
      -webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; overflow-x: hidden;
    }
    html[data-page="BT"] :where(a) { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
    /* The design's global link hover: every link without its own hover turns red. */
    html[data-page="BT"] :where(a:hover) { color: var(--accent-text); }
    /* text-transform is DECLARED, not defaulted: an unscoped uppercase heading
       rule in another family's global block once capitalised every template. */
    html[data-page="BT"] :where(h1,h2,h3,h4,p,figure,blockquote,dl,dd,ol,ul) { margin: 0; }
    html[data-page="BT"] :where(h1,h2,h3,h4) { text-transform: none; }
    html[data-page="BT"] :where(summary) { list-style: none; cursor: pointer; }
    html[data-page="BT"] summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }

    /* ── layout scaffolding ───────────────────────────────────────────── */
    html[data-page="BT"] :where(.wrap) {
      max-width: var(--maxw); margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 var(--gutter);
    }

    /* ── .eyebrow — 13px tracked caps in red; marigold on an ink band ─── */
    html[data-page="BT"] :where(.eyebrow) {
      margin: 0; font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 13px; font-weight: 700;
      letter-spacing: .14em; text-transform: uppercase; color: var(--accent-text);
      overflow-wrap: anywhere;
    }

    /* ── .ph — a photo. The frame IS the image: a cover-fitted background on
          the element that carries data-image-field. Sections size it; the
          blush ground only shows while a photo loads. A section OMITS the
          element when the owner supplied no photo. */
    html[data-page="BT"] :where(.ph) {
      background-color: var(--paper-2);
      background-size: cover; background-position: center; background-repeat: no-repeat;
      overflow: hidden;
    }

    /* ── BUTTONS (the design's inline styles, verbatim metrics) ──────── */
    html[data-page="BT"] :where(.btn) {
      background-color: transparent;
      display: inline-flex; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
      min-height: 54px; padding: 0 26px; border-radius: 14px;
      border: 2px solid transparent;
      font-family: var(--sans); font-size: 15px; font-weight: 700; line-height: 1.6;
      letter-spacing: normal; text-transform: none; text-decoration: none;
      text-align: center; cursor: pointer;
    }
    /* red fill, the design's primary */
    html[data-page="BT"] :where(.btn--fill) { background-color: var(--accent); border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--on-primary); }
    html[data-page="BT"] :where(.btn--fill:hover) { background-color: var(--ink); border-color: var(--ink); color: var(--paper); }
    /* outline on a light ground */
    html[data-page="BT"] :where(.btn--line) { background-color: transparent; border-color: var(--ink); color: var(--ink); }
    html[data-page="BT"] :where(.btn--line:hover) { background-color: var(--ink); border-color: var(--ink); color: var(--paper); }
    /* marigold fill, the action on an ink band */
    html[data-page="BT"] :where(.btn--mari) { background-color: var(--accent-light); border-color: var(--accent-light); color: var(--ink); }
    html[data-page="BT"] :where(.btn--mari:hover) { background-color: var(--paper); border-color: var(--paper); color: var(--ink); }
    /* ink fill, the action on a marigold band */
    html[data-page="BT"] :where(.btn--ink) { background-color: var(--ink); border-color: var(--ink); color: var(--paper); }
    html[data-page="BT"] :where(.btn--ink:hover) { background-color: var(--accent); border-color: var(--accent); color: var(--on-primary); }
    /* paper fill, the action inside the ink location card */
    html[data-page="BT"] :where(.btn--paper) { background-color: var(--paper); border-color: var(--paper); color: var(--ink); }
    html[data-page="BT"] :where(.btn--paper:hover) { background-color: var(--accent-light); border-color: var(--accent-light); color: var(--ink); }

    /* ── FOCUS · the duo ring (fact 3) ─────────────────────────────────── */
    html[data-page="BT"] :where(a,button,summary,[tabindex]):focus-visible {
      outline: 3px solid var(--paper); outline-offset: 0;
      box-shadow: 0 0 0 6px var(--ink);
    }

    /* ── skip link ────────────────────────────────────────────────────── */
    html[data-page="BT"] :where(.skip) {
      position: absolute; left: -999px; top: 0; z-index: 100;
      background-color: var(--ink); color: var(--paper);
      padding: 12px 18px; border-radius: 0 0 14px 0;
      font-family: var(--sans); font-weight: 700; font-size: 15px;
    }
    html[data-page="BT"] :where(.skip:focus) { left: 0; top: 0; }
  </style>

  <style is:global set:html={__schemeCss}></style>
  {__fontHref && <link href={__fontHref} rel="stylesheet" />}
  <style is:global set:html={__overrideCss}></style>
</head>
<body>
  <a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to content</a>
  <HeaderBT layout={layout} content={content} />
  <main id="main">
    {visibility.heroSection !== false && <HeroBT content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.marqueeBlock !== false && <MarqueeBT content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.trustBlock !== false && <TrustBT content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.servicesSection !== false && <ServicesBT content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.aboutSection !== false && <AboutBT content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.whyUsBlock !== false && <WhyBT content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.gallerySection !== false && <GalleryBT content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.howItWorksBlock !== false && <HowBT content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.testimonialsBlock !== false && <TestimonialsBT content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.credentialsBlock !== false && <CredentialsBT content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.serviceAreaBlock !== false && <AreaBT content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.faqBlock !== false && <FaqBT content={content} layout={layout} />}
    {visibility.locationBlock !== false && <LocationBT content={content} layout={layout} />}
  </main>
  {visibility.ctaBandBlock !== false && <CtaBandBT content={content} layout={layout} />}
  <FooterBT layout={layout} content={content} />

  <script is:inline src="https://unpkg.com/leaflet@1.9.4/dist/leaflet.js" integrity="sha256-20nQCchB9co0qIjJZRGuk2/Z9VM+kNiyxNV1lvTlZBo=" crossorigin=""></script>
  <script is:inline>
    (function () {
      // BT Leaflet boot — (lat, lng, label) from LocationBT. The
      // global name is family-unique on purpose: a preview harness can render
      // two wrappers in one document, and a shared name cross-wires the maps.
      window.__floristBTInitMap = function (lat, lng, label) {
        if (!window.L) return;
        var el = document.getElementById('map'); if (!el) return;
        if (el._leaflet_id) return;
        // Erases LocationBT's drawn fallback face; without this the tiles
        // stack on top of it.
        el.innerHTML = '';
        var map = L.map('map', { scrollWheelZoom: false }).setView([lat, lng], 16);
        // lib/carto.ts appends the CARTO key to this exact URL at publish time.
        L.tileLayer('https://basemaps.cartocdn.com/rastertiles/voyager/{z}/{x}/{y}{r}.png', { attribution: '&copy; OpenStreetMap &copy; CARTO', maxZoom: 19, subdomains: 'abcd' }).addTo(map);
        // The design's pin: a red dot, an ink rim and a marigold halo. The
        // colours are READ from the live tokens, so an admin colour pick
        // recolours the pin too (the engine sets them on this same element).
        var cs = window.getComputedStyle(document.documentElement);
        var red = (cs.getPropertyValue('--accent') || '').trim() || '#C21E3A';
        var ink = (cs.getPropertyValue('--ink') || '').trim() || '#2B1015';
        var sun = (cs.getPropertyValue('--accent-light') || '').trim() || '#F2B233';
        var icon = L.divIcon({
          className: '',
          html: '<div style="width:22px;height:22px;border-radius:50%;background:' + red + ';border:3px solid ' + ink + ';box-shadow:0 0 0 3px ' + sun + '"></div>',
          iconSize: [22, 22], iconAnchor: [11, 11]
        });
        L.marker([lat, lng], { icon: icon, keyboard: false }).addTo(map);
      };
      // Drain LocationBT's hand-off. This script runs only after leaflet.js
      // above has loaded (or failed — then the init returns and the drawn face
      // stays), so a slow download can never outlast the boot.
      if (window.__floristBTMapArgs) window.__floristBTInitMap.apply(null, window.__floristBTMapArgs);
    })();
  </script>
</body>
</html>
